{"abstract":"Bio-hybrid systems-close couplings of natural organisms with technology-are high potential and still underexplored. In existing work, robots have mostly influenced group behaviors of animals. We explore the possibilities of mixing robots with natural plants, merging useful attributes. Significant synergies arise by combining the plants' ability to efficiently produce shaped material and the robots' ability to extend sensing and decision-making behaviors. However, programming robots to control plant motion and shape requires good knowledge of complex plant behaviors. Therefore, we use machine learning to create a holistic plant model and evolve robot controllers. As a benchmark task we choose obstacle avoidance. We use computer vision to construct a model of plant stem stiffening and motion dynamics by training an LSTM network. The LSTM network acts as a forward model predicting change in the plant, driving the evolution of neural network robot controllers. The evolved controllers augment the plants' natural light-finding and tissue-stiffening behaviors to avoid obstacles and grow desired shapes. We successfully verify the robot controllers and bio-hybrid behavior in reality, with a physical setup and actual plants.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wahby, Mostafa","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Zahadat, Payam","Risi, Sebastian","Ayres, Phil","Schmickl, Thomas","Hamann, Heiko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383404"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio hybrid systems","Machine learning","Neural network controllers","Obstacle avoidance","Plant robot interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robot to shape your natural plant the machine learning approach to model and control bio hybrid systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83680870/1804.06682.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383404","identifier":[{"id":"85050634013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-915ec9d9-a957-4b7a-b576-ead3874aa79c"],"keyword":["Bio-hybrid systems","Machine learning","Neural network controllers","Obstacle avoidance","Plant-robot interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88BDB2A5AE07DD362D01B8D09AE12F9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83680870/1804.06682.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","locid":"8785f18a-1bf3-4c63-8d8b-d3e5d516ca40","name":"Zahadat, Payam","orcid":"0000-0002-4521-7428","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","name":"Ayres, Phil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmicklpau","last":"Schmickl","name":"Schmickl, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3205455.3205516","isbn":["9781450356183"],"pages":"165-172","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Conference on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation (GECCO 2018)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050634013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-915ec9d9-a957-4b7a-b576-ead3874aa79c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Robot to Shape your Natural Plant: The Machine Learning Approach to Model and Control Bio-Hybrid Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383404","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Key to our project flora robotica is the idea of creating a bio-hybrid system of tightly coupled natural plants and distributed robots to grow architectural artifacts and spaces. Our motivation with this ground research project is to lay a principled foundation towards the design and implementation of living architectural systems that provide functionalities beyond those of orthodox building practice, such as self-repair, material accumulation and self-organization. Plants and robots work together to create a living organism that is inhabited by human beings. User-defined design objectives help to steer the directional growth of the plants, but also the system's interactions with its inhabitants determine locations where growth is prohibited or desired (e.g., partitions, windows, occupiable space). We report our plant species selection process and aspects of living architecture. A leitmotif of our project is the rich concept of braiding: braids are produced by robots from continuous material and serve as both scaffolds and initial architectural artifacts before plants take over and grow the desired architecture. We use light and hormones as attraction stimuli and far-red light as repelling stimulus to influence the plants. Applied sensors range from simple proximity sensing to detect the presence of plants to sophisticated sensing technology, such as electrophysiology and measurements of sap flow. We conclude by discussing our anticipated final demonstrator that integrates key features of flora robotica, such as the continuous growth process of architectural artifacts and self-repair of living architecture.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Divband Soorati, Mohammad","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Kuksin, Igor","Veenstra, Frank","Wahby, Mostafa","Nielsen, Stig Anton","Risi, Sebastian","Skrzypczak, Tomasz","Zahadat, Payam","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw","Støy, Kasper","Schmickl, Thomas","Kernbach, Serge","Ayres, Phil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126277"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-04","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2017-09-04","title":"Living Architectures Workshop 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica an architectural system combining living natural plants and distributed robots","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.04291","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126277","ids":["arkc-23766292-0a13-4a7c-85f6-d872d12b7052"],"keyword":["No"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DCD81E7B6B7AE9AFEF6564EB83A02550"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.04291","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"cybertronica ug","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"pl","key":"adam mickiewicz university","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Adam Mickiewicz University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"divbandsooratipau","last":"Divband Soorati","name":"Divband Soorati, Mohammad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Igor","key":"kuksinpau","last":"Kuksin","name":"Kuksin, Igor","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Anton","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Stig Anton","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"skrzypczakpau","last":"Skrzypczak","name":"Skrzypczak, Tomasz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","name":"Zahadat, Payam","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Przemyslaw","key":"wojtaszekpau","last":"Wojtaszek","name":"Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","name":"Støy, Kasper","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmicklpau","last":"Schmickl","name":"Schmickl, Thomas","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Serge","key":"kernbachpau","last":"Kernbach","name":"Kernbach, Serge","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","locid":"809e3672-ddc8-44e7-8a1b-1c1309974305","name":"Ayres, Phil","orcid":"0000-0002-9266-065X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","subtitle":"the 14th European Conference on Artificial Life","title":"Proceedings of ECAL 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-23766292-0a13-4a7c-85f6-d872d12b7052"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Flora robotica -- An Architectural System Combining Living Natural Plants and Distributed Robots","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126277","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Mixing societies of natural and artificial systems can provide interesting and potentially fruitful research targets. Here we mix robotic setups and natural plants in order to steer the motion behavior of plants while growing. The robotic setup uses a camera to observe the plant and uses a pair of light sources to trigger phototropic response, steering the plant to user-defined targets. An evolutionary robotic approach is used to design a controller for the setup. Initially, preliminary experiments are performed with a simple predetermined controller and a growing bean plant. The plant behavior in response to the simple controller is captured by image processing, and a model of the plant tip dynamics is developed. The model is used in simulation to evolve a robot controller that steers the plant tip such that it follows a number of randomly generated target points. Finally, we test the simulation-evolved controller in the real setup controlling a natural bean plant. The results demonstrate a successful crossing of the reality gap in the setup. The success of the approach allows for future extensions to more complex tasks including control of the shape of plants and pattern formation in multiple plant setups.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Wahby, Mostafa","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Hamann, Heiko","Zahadat, Payam","Ayres, Phil","Schmickl, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-127108"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolved control of natural plants crossing the reality gap for user defined steering of growth and motion","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3124643","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-127108","identifier":[{"id":"85030213419","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-6da11fc1-f0c9-4339-9bb7-5455ba22f070"],"keyword":["No"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6445347083891A8E67010A3EAFF03A48"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3124643","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","name":"Zahadat, Payam","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","locid":"809e3672-ddc8-44e7-8a1b-1c1309974305","name":"Ayres, Phil","orcid":"0000-0002-9266-065X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmicklpau","last":"Schmickl","name":"Schmickl, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3124643","issn":["15564665","15564703"],"issn_org":["15564665"],"issue":"3","journal":"ACM Transactions on Autonomous and Adaptive Systems","paperid":"15","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Autonomous and Adaptive Systems","title_org":"ACM Transactions on Autonomous and Adaptive Systems (TAAS)","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030213419"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-6da11fc1-f0c9-4339-9bb7-5455ba22f070"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Evolved Control of Natural Plants: Crossing the Reality Gap for User-Defined Steering of Growth and Motion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-127108","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Self-organized construction with continuous, structured building material, as opposed to modular units, offers new challenges to the robot-based construction process and lends the opportunity for increased flexibility in constructed artifact properties, such as shape and deformation. As an example investigation, we look at continuous filaments organized into braided structures, within the context of bio-hybrids constructing architectural artifacts. We report the result of an early swarm robot experiment. The robots successfully constructed a braid in a self-organized process. The construction process can be extended by using different materials and by embedding sensors during the self-organized construction directly into the braided structure. In future work, we plan to apply dedicated braiding robot hardware and to construct sophisticated 3-d structures with local variability in patterns of filament interlacing.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Wahby, Mostafa","Divband Soorati, Mohammad","Nicolas Hofstadler, Daniel","Zahadat, Payam","Ayres, Phil","Støy, Kasper","Hamann, Heiko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126248"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-16","start":"2016-09-12","title":"2016 IEEE","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self organized construction with continuous building material higher flexibility based on braided structures","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/62353185/Self_Organized_Construction_with_Continuous_Building_Material_Higher_Flexibility_based_on_Braided_Structures.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126248","identifier":[{"id":"85011076110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-21338902-87f5-4db4-83c1-11c12355bd9e"],"keyword":["No"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6F4C3D464DA0EC949D1AB6FC4176571C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/62353185/Self_Organized_Construction_with_Continuous_Building_Material_Higher_Flexibility_based_on_Braided_Structures.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"divbandsooratipau","last":"Divband Soorati","name":"Divband Soorati, Mohammad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"nicolashofstadlerpau","last":"Nicolas Hofstadler","name":"Nicolas Hofstadler, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","name":"Zahadat, Payam","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","locid":"809e3672-ddc8-44e7-8a1b-1c1309974305","name":"Ayres, Phil","orcid":"0000-0002-9266-065X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","name":"Støy, Kasper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"154-159","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 1st International Workshop on Self-Organising Construction (SOCO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-21338902-87f5-4db4-83c1-11c12355bd9e"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Self-Organized Construction with Continuous Building Material : Higher Flexibility based on Braided Structures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126248","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The self-organizing bio-hybrid collaboration of robots and natural plants allows for a variety of interesting applications. As an example we investigate how robots can be used to control the growth and motion of a natural plant, using LEDs to provide stimuli. We follow an evolutionary robotics approach where task performance is determined by monitoring the plant's reaction. First, we do initial plant experiments with simple, predetermined controllers. Then we use image sampling data as a model of the dynamics of the plant tip xy position. Second, we use this approach to evolve robot controllers in simulation. The task is to make the plant approach three predetermined, distinct points in an xy-plane. Finally, we test the evolved controllers in real plant experiments and find that we cross the reality gap successfully. We shortly describe how we have extended from plant tip to many points on the plant, for a model of the plant stem dynamics. Future work will extend to two-axes image sampling for a 3-d approach.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wahby, Mostafa","Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Zahadat, Payam","Hamann, Heiko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-128606"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-16","place":"Augsburg, de","start":"2016-09-12","title":"Self-Adaptive and Self-Organizing Systems (SASO), 2016 IEEE 10th International Conference on","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"keyword":["Bio hybrid","Evolutionary Robotics","Self organization"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an evolutionary robotics approach to the control of plant growth and motion modeling plants and crossing the reality gap","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/311419851_An_Evolutionary_Robotics_Approach_to_the_Control_of_Plant_Growth_and_Motion_Modeling_Plants_and_Crossing_the_Reality_Gap","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-128606","identifier":[{"id":"85010304105","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-eb5c7b20-d7a1-4749-8fed-e5ec98b5ec87"],"keyword":["Bio-hybrid","No","evolutionary robotics","plant modeling","reality gap","self-organization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-258ADF350FC1DF6D9D5C8760F682E4B6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","name":"Zahadat, Payam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/saso.2016.8","eisbn":["9781509035342"],"isbn":["9781509035359"],"status":"p","title":"Self-Adaptive and Self-Organizing Systems (SASO), 2016 IEEE 10th International Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010304105"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-eb5c7b20-d7a1-4749-8fed-e5ec98b5ec87"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"An Evolutionary Robotics Approach to the Control of Plant Growth and Motion: Modeling Plants and Crossing the Reality Gap","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-128606","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Besides the life-as-it-could-be driver of artificial life research there is also the concept of extending natural life by creating hybrids or mixed societies that are built from natural and artificial components. In this paper we motivate and present the research program of the project flora robotica. Our objective is to develop and to investigate closely linked symbiotic relationships between robots and natural plants and to explore the potentials of a plant-robot society able to produce architectural artifacts and living spaces. These robot-plant bio-hybrids create synergies that allow for new functions of plants and robots. They also create novel design opportunities for an architecture that fuses the design and construction phase. The bio-hybrid is an example of mixed societies between ‘hard artificial and ‘wet natural life, which enables an interaction between natural and artificial ecologies. They form an embodied, self-organizing, and distributed cognitive system which is supposed to grow and develop over long periods of time resulting in the creation of meaningful architectural structures. A key idea is to assign equal roles to robots and plants in order to create a highly integrated, symbiotic system. Besides the gain of knowledge, this project has the objective to create a bio-hybrid system with a defined function and application – growing architectural artifacts.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Wahby, Mostafa","Schmickl, Thomas","Zahadat, Payam","Hofstadler, Daniel","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian","Faina, Andres","Veenstra, Frank","Kernbach, Serge","Kuksin, Igor","Kernbach, Olga","Ayers, Phil","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw"],"cuid":["S02-089.67-012432"],"event":{"acronym":"IEEE SSCI","end":"2015-12-10","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2015-12-07","title":"2015 IEEE Symposium on Artifical Life","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"keyword":["Architecture","Artificial Life","Bio hybrid","Bio hybrid systems","Plants","Robots","Self organizing systems","architectural artifacts","plant robot symbiosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica mixed societies of symbiotic robot plant bio hybrids","src":["arkc","itu"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.67-012432","identifier":[{"id":"84964937762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-8a5ce1d1-e2e0-4c7d-9e51-2001d8744f9a","itu-4181dddd-1be3-4361-8109-ca1419e73d88"],"keyword":["Architecture","Bio-hybrid","No","Plants","Robots","architectural artifacts","artificial life","bio-hybrid systems","plant-robot symbiosis","self-organizing systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB54DC9B986B7E29B1E706A371F1092E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80993764/IEEE_ALIFE_2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"it